---
// Search and enquiry measurement (docs/seo/measurement.md).
//
// Nothing is sent anywhere unless the owner sets PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID
// (a Google Analytics 4 "G-…" ID) in the deployment's environment. Without
// it this only defines window.fpTrack, which announces each event on the
// page (a "fp:track" DOM event) and does no network request.
//
// Events. Page visits come from GA4's own page_view. On top of it:
//   view_item_list         a collection page was opened ([data-track-list])
//   view_item              a product page was opened ([data-track-item])
//   whatsapp_enquiry_click a direct WhatsApp enquiry link or button was used
//   basket_quote_request   the basket was sent on WhatsApp (sent by cart.astro)
// Each carries the page path, the session's landing path (path only, no
// query), a category and — where there is one — the design code or product
// slug, and the recipient city (a registry slug such as "mumbai") when the
// visitor has chosen one or is on a city page. The city is where the flowers
// are going, not where the visitor is. An enquiry is a click, not an order:
// completed orders are recorded by hand (scripts/seo/report.mjs).
//
// A visit that arrives from a known AI assistant is labelled once per session
// as ai_referrer ("chatgpt", "perplexity", "copilot", "gemini", "claude"),
// from the referring hostname alone, or from a utm_source that is exactly one
// of those hostnames. Nothing else of the referrer or the URL is read or
// kept: no path, no query, no prompt. A visit with no referrer is direct,
// never "AI"; a google.com referrer is Google Search, and is not counted as
// Google's AI features, which cannot be told apart this way.
//
// Never sent: names, phone numbers, addresses, recipient details, card
// messages or the WhatsApp message text.
const measurementId = (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID ?? "").trim();
const enabled = /^G-[A-Z0-9]{4,}$/.test(measurementId);

// The tracking code is reviewed source (src/scripts/inline/analytics.js),
// allowed by the page's CSP through its hash. The only value added to it is
// the validated build-time measurement ID, as a JSON string literal.
import InlineScript from "./InlineScript.astro";
import analyticsSource from "../scripts/inline/analytics.js?raw";
const analyticsCode = `(function () {\nvar measurementId = ${JSON.stringify(enabled ? measurementId : "")};\n${analyticsSource}})();\n`;
---

{enabled && <script is:inline async src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${measurementId}`}></script>}
<InlineScript code={analyticsCode} />
